===Etymology 1===
From {{etyl|enm|en}} {{m|enm|fey||fated to die}}, from {{etyl|ang|en}} {{m|ang|fǣge||doomed to die, timid}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|en}} {{m|gem-pro|*faigijaz||cowardly, wicked}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|en}} {{m|ine-pro|*pAik-}}, {{m|ine-pro|*pAig-||ill-meaning, bad}}. Akin to {{cog|osx|fēgi}} whence {{cog|nl|veeg||doomed, near death}}, {{cog|goh|feigi||appointed for death, ungodly}} whence {{cog|de|feige||cowardly}}, {{cog|non|feigr||doomed}} whence the Icelandic {{m|is|feigur||doomed to die}}, {{cog|ang|fāh||outlawed, hostile}}. More at {{l|en|foe}}.

